{{!--
	Trait body. One root element, as the framework requires of every PART.

	An ability, a disability or an immunity -- one type separated by a category, because they
	are one shape in his data.

	The two values are text on purpose. What they mean changes from entry to entry: for Frost
	Sensitivity they are a magic-resistance penalty and extra damage per die, and for Acid
	Resistant a damage multiplier and a resistance bonus. A trait does not apply them itself;
	the description is what the table reads.
--}}
<section class="imagine-item-body trait">

	<div class="panel-row">
		<div class="panel">
			<h3>Kind</h3>
			<ul class="band-list">
				<li><label>Category</label>
					<span><select name="system.category">
						{{#each config.categories as |c|}}
						<option value="{{c}}" {{#if (eq c ../system.category)}}selected{{/if}}>{{c}}</option>
						{{/each}}
					</select></span></li>
			</ul>
			<p class="muted">The canonical name is what his sheet displays when the entry is looked up
			by a different spelling &mdash; "Acid Regeneration" resolves to "Regeneration(Acid)".</p>
		</div>
	</div>

	{{!-- Was a band-list row, ~90px wide, sized for "Regeneration(Acid)". His longest canonical
	      name runs to 44 characters ("Prehensile Tentacles With Prehensile Fingers"), which the
	      band-list clipped to about a dozen visible characters -- Daryl's screenshot showed
	      "Energy(Complete)" cut to "Energy(Compl". Moved to a wide-field, the same fix the race
	      sheet's skill note got for the same reason, with the full value also on the title
	      attribute for a still-longer future entry. --}}
	<label class="wide-field">Canonical name
		<input type="text" name="system.canonicalName" value="{{system.canonicalName}}"
			placeholder="{{item.name}}" title="{{system.canonicalName}}"></label>

	<div class="panel-row">
		<div class="panel">
			<h3>Values</h3>
			<ul class="band-list">
				<li><label>Value 1</label>
					<span><input type="text" name="system.value1" value="{{system.value1}}" placeholder="&mdash;"></span></li>
				<li><label>Value 2</label>
					<span><input type="text" name="system.value2" value="{{system.value2}}" placeholder="&mdash;"></span></li>
			</ul>
			<p class="muted">Their meaning is per entry rather than per column, so they are text. Nothing
			reads them automatically.</p>
		</div>
	</div>

	<h3 class="section-head">Description</h3>
	<textarea name="system.description" rows="6">{{system.description}}</textarea>
</section>
